cludes making our delivery pace sustainable through stable releases, a well-maintained codebase and engineering practices that scale with the business. The role carries a clear mandate to shape how engineering works at Sunday.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will own</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People leadership: development plans, performance conversations against clear role expectations, hiring and onboarding. You hold conversations early and directly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering ways of working: code review standards, quality gates before release, build and release pipeline, and a deliberate plan to reduce hotfixes and technical debt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architecture and platform: owning the technical foundations shared across our games, including our in house SDK, analytics tracking, live configuration and the setup of A/B tests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delivery partnership: working with the producers who lead our cross functional game teams on estimates, capacity and technical risk, and having the final say on whether a release is technically ready to ship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transparency: making engineering progress, quality and capacity visible to the rest of the company through clear, measurable indicators.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least four years managing an engineering team of five or more people, including performance management and hiring.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong engineering background of your own, ideally in C#, Unity or mobile development, so you can lead architecture and review decisions with credibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of success in a commercially driven company operating live products with real users, 