&lt;p&gt;This job description was written by humans, assisted by AI. We may leverage technology in our hiring process to help us see the person behind the resume.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coveo is committed to providing accessible employment practices. If you require accommodation due to a disability at any point during the recruitment process, please contact ----- to discuss your needs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#li-hybrid&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/coveoen/senior-technical-project-manager-174108","tags":["Professional Services"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792922114},{"slug":"senior-partner-success-manager-emea-london-93903","company_name":"G2","title":"Senior Partner Success Manager, EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About G2 - The Company</strong><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">G2 is the world's largest and most trusted software marketplace. When you join G2, you’re joining the industry’s leading team that helps businesses reach their peak potential by powering decisions and strategies with trusted insights from real software users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we have joined forces with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.capterra.com/"><u>Capterra</u></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.softwareadvice.com/"><u>SoftwareAdvice</u></a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getapp.com/"><u>GetApp</u></a> to create the largest source of online data and software insights to fuel intelligent buying in the age of AI. With 200M+ combined annual visitors and 6M verified reviews, we are now the centralized place to enable software buyers to make better and faster decisions with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And we are just getting started! We are setting out to transform the global B2B software industry and become the most trusted data foundation for buyers and sellers of software for the age of AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Does that sound exciting to you? Come join us as we try to reach our next PEAK!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About G2 - Our People</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At G2, everything we are and what we do is grounded in our  PEAK values— (<em>P</em>erformance + <em>E</em>ntrepreneurship + <em>A</em>uthenticity + <em>K</em>indness. Working at G2 means you are part of a value-driven, growing global community that climbs PEAKs together. We cheer for each other’s successes, learn from our mistakes, and support and lean on one another during challenging times. With ambition and entrepreneurial spirit we push each other to take on challenging work, which will help us all to grow and learn.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be part of a global, diverse team of smart, dedicated, and kind individuals - each with unique talents, aspirations, and life experiences. At the heart of our community and culture are our people-led ERGs, which celebrate and highlight the diverse identities of our global team. As an organization, we are intentional about our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://company.g2.com/dei"><u>DEI</u></a> and philanthropic work (like our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://company.g2.com/gives"><u>G2 Gives</u></a> program) because it encourages us all to be better people.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As G2’s only Partner Manager based in EMEA, your mission is to expand the impact of G2’s most strategic partners to EMEA, building real influence with the EMEA based revenue and marketing leaders and their orgs at G2’s strategic integration, agency and channel partners.  You'll drive inbound co-sell activity to our field and collaborate with G2’s revenue org to effectively activate partners in their deal and renewal cycles.  You will also extend this internal work to G2’s field in APAC</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of this role, you’ll work to grow EMEA based relationships and revenue with newly established Ads partners, a growing revenue segment at G2, and a select set of agency partners you will prioritize as having the highest leverage for pipeline generation and revenue in the region.  Core to this role is the ability to work globally with the North American based team to understand and extend the global strategy for the partners you’re activating in EMEA, while also partnering very closely with EMEA based revenue leaders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>In This Role, You Will: </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and Expand Partner Relationships to Grow Influence Across G2</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop genuine influence with EMEA-based revenue and marketing leaders at partner organizations, establishing yourself as the regional counterpart for partners whose primary relationship with G2 has historically been run from North America.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the North American partner team to understand and extend the global strategy for each partner you activate, while providing regional insight that shapes how those strategies land in EMEA &amp; APAC.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with G2’s EMEA revenue leaders and field teams to activate partners in live deals and renewal cycles, ensuring partner involvement is timely, relevant, and tied to specific accounts and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with partner-side Sales, Marketing, and Enablement teams in the region to launch joint offers, map shared accounts, and deliver customer-facing education on our joint value, adapting messaging to local market dynamics, languages, and buying behaviors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with CS leadership in region to drive adoption of integrations among EMEA &amp; APAC customers to increase renewal and expansion, and extend partner use cases (e.g., MCP Connectors, data package installations) across G2’s most strategic integration partners in the region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and analyze EMEA partner performance to optimize program impact, and provide regular updates to leadership on adoption rates, pipeline contribution, and revenue impact by region and partner.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner Development</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop a select set of new partner relationships that have high leverage for EMEA &amp; APAC pipeline and revenue.  Manage development end-to-end, from initial conversations through commercials, GTM planning, and activation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed G2 within partner revenue teams, building the relationships and cadence needed to keep G2 top of mind as a growth lever for them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure G2's internal teams understand the value each partner brings and how to activate them to drive revenue for their own books of business.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be a Subject Matter Expert on G2’s integration capabilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build rapport with sales and partners as an expert on G2 and our partner ecosystem</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create leverage on the Partnership team by consistently sharing new learnings and industry insights</p></li></ul><h2></h2><h2>Minimum Qualifications:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We realize applying for jobs can feel daunting at times. Even if you don’t check all the boxes in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in tech-related partnerships, sales, or customer success, with a track record of developing senior and executive-level relationships across partner revenue, marketing, and product organizations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to understand and effectively communicate the basic mechanics and shared value of G2’s integrations with our most strategic partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience developing and scaling partnerships globally, with a track record of consistently delivering strong adoption and revenue growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong prospecting and relationship-building skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with ambiguity, bringing innovation and good judgment to fast-paced, quickly changing environments, and knowing when to bring structure and process as we grow and adapt to a shifting market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional relationship management, collaboration, and communication skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A self-starter who exhibits passion, persistence, and drive in your work. </p></li></ul><h3>What Can Help Your Application Stand Out:</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in adtech, some knowledge and comfort level  navigating conversations with publishers and DSPs </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the Office</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">London is home to our EMEA headquarters. The London office has a strong in-office culture and meet frequently in person to collaborate and win together. Because of this, we prefer candidates who are interested in going into the office 2-3 days a week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Commitment to Inclusivity and Diversity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At G2, we are committed to creating an inclusive and diverse environment where people of every background can thrive and feel welcome. We consider applicants without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, genetic information, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, age, or marital, veteran, or physical or mental disability status. Learn more about our commitments <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://culture.g2.com/commitments"><u>here</u></a>. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">--</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />For job applicants in California, the United Kingdom, and the European Union, please review <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.g2.com/applicant-privacy-notice"><u>this applicant privacy notice</u></a> before applying to this job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Use AI Technology in Our Hiring Process</strong><br />G2 incorporates AI-powered technology to enhance our candidate evaluation process. These tools may assist with initial application screening, skills assessment analysis, and identifying candidates whose qualifications align with specific role requirements. While AI technology supports our recruitment workflow, all final hiring decisions remain under human oversight and judgment.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Choice Matters:</strong> If you would prefer that your application be reviewed without AI assistance, you can opt out by entering your email address in the email entry field at the bottom of the Automated Processing Legal Notice. Choosing to opt out will not disadvantage your application in any way—we will ensure your materials receive a thorough manual review by our hiring team.<br />For additional details about how we handle your information throughout the application process, please review <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" href="https://legal.g2.com/applicant-privacy-notice">G2's Applicant Privacy Notice</a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/g2/senior-partner-success-manager-emea-london-93903","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792921217},{"slug":"remote-solutions-architect-158679","company_name":"Livekit","title":"Solutions Architect","description":"<h2>ABOUT LIVEKIT</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">LiveKit is building the infrastructure layer for the agentic era of computing. Our platform gives developers everything they need to build, test, deploy, scale, and observe AI agents in production. Founded in 2021, LiveKit powers voice and agentic AI applications for OpenAI, Salesforce, Spotify, Meta, and tens of thousands of other developers, collectively facilitating billions of calls each year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>ABOUT THIS ROLE</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a Solutions Architect (Pre-Sales) to be the technical partner to the engineers and enterprises building on LiveKit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work alongside an account executive to understand what a customer is trying to build, design the right architecture, and bring it to life with live demos and proofs-of-concept — guiding teams from first conversation to production.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is ideal for someone who loves to build, is energized by talking with other engineers, and takes pride in turning a hard technical problem into something that just works. Real-time voice and video is visceral — latency, quality, and reliability are felt, not read about — so the best conversations include something live. You'll collaborate closely with our Sales, Engineering, Product teams to win technical decisions and to make sure what you hear in the field informs how we build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>YOU'LL THRIVE HERE IF YOU:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">love to build and solve the most challenging customer problems with LiveKit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">have a curious mind with a continuous desire to learn and improve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">enjoy demoing and presenting, whether to a room of engineer,  to a CTO or at a conference</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">have a team first mentally, seeking to lift others around you as you progress in your career</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHAT YOU'LL DO</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with an account executive as the technical lead on strategic deals — from discovery and architecture design through demos, POCs, and technical decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise customers on cloud architecture and deployment across self-hosted and LiveKit Cloud (AWS, GCP, Azure)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build live demos and reference applications — voice agents, video pipelines, telephony integrations — tailored to each customer's use case, and reusable by the wider team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope and run proofs-of-concept against clear, shared success criteria, guiding customers all the way to production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reason with customers about connectivity, infrastructure, and end-to-end latency to design for scale and reliability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create technical content — blog posts, guides, webinars, and conference talks — that helps developers and enterprises build with LiveKit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the technical enabler for your region's pod, and share field insight with Product and Engineering to help shape the roadmap</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHO YOU ARE</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4+ years in solutions architecture, sales engineering, or a customer-facing engineering role (or equivalent hands-on engineering experience with strong customer instincts)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with at least one major cloud provider (AWS, GCP, or Azure) — you can architect, deploy, and debug real applications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with the modern deployment toolchain: containers, Kubernetes, infrastructure-as-code, and networking fundamentals (load balancing, DNS, firewalls/NAT)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to reason about connectivity, infrastructure, and latency end to end — how architecture, network path, compute, co-location, and model choice shape the AI agentic experiences of today</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong programming ability in at least one of our core SDK languages — Python, TypeScript/Node, or Go</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear communicator who can demo, present, and write for technical audiences</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of real-time media protocols and their latency/quality trade-offs (WebRTC, RTP/SRTP, WebSockets)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with the AI voice stack: STT/TTS providers, LLM integration, speech-to-speech models, turn detection, and telephony/SIP</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience speaking at meetups or conferences, or a track record of technical writing or open-source contributions</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>OUR COMMITMENT TO YOU</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An opportunity to build something truly impactful to the world</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to open source alongside world-class engineers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary and equity package</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible vacation policy</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">LiveKit is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any characteristic protected by applicable law. If you require a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please contact <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- £160K – £240K • Offers Equity • The range above is On-Target Earnings (OTE), split 70% base salary and 30% variable, and covers multiple levels. Where you land depends on experience and the level we hire at.</p><ul><li> • Solutions Engineer £160K – £240K • Offers Equity • The range above is On-Target Earnings (OTE), split 70% base salary and 30% variable, and covers multiple levels. Where you land depends on experience and the level we hire at.</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/livekit/remote-solutions-architect-158679","tags":["S&M"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom (Remote)","created_at":1792921216},{"slug":"senior-partner-deployed-engineer-united-kingdom-286644","company_name":"Coder","title":"Senior Partner Deployed Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Senior Partner Deployed Engineer to join the Customer Solutions team, focused on building Coder’s partner ecosystem across EMEA. This is a new function at Coder, modeled on the Forward Deployed Engineer role pioneered by companies like Palantir and now the fastest-growing technical role at frontier AI companies. The difference: instead of embedding with a single customer to deploy a platform, you embed with strategic partners to help them understand, position, and deliver Coder’s platform across their entire customer base.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are part Field CTO, part Industry Strategist, part Technical Specialist, and part Partner Relations Lead. You will be the technical authority within our EMEA partner ecosystem: setting the vision for how Coder fits into each partner’s AI, cloud, and modernization offerings, co-creating the GTM sales plays that partner sellers take to market, building the demonstrations and workshops that generate pipeline, and producing the Partner Relations content that establishes Coder’s technical brand in the ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a support role. You are equally comfortable holding a strategic roadmap conversation with a partner CTO and debugging a Kubernetes deployment in a partner’s lab in the same afternoon. You are energized by the challenge of building a new category through partnerships, motivated by the multiplied impact of enabling an entire ecosystem rather than a single customer, and capable of operating with full autonomy in a fast-moving startup environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the strategic technical thought partner to EMEA partner leadership, including practice leads, CTOs, and solutions architects at global systems integrators, regional cloud consultancies, and hyperscaler field teams. Own the technical relationship and set the vision for how Coder fits into each partner’s AI and modernization portfolio.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-create sales plays tailored to each partner’s customer base, vertical focus, and services capabilities. Author Working Backwards outcome proposals for strategic partner-customer combinations that translate AI Development Infrastructure into deal-level urgency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and deliver workshops, Builder Labs, and partner-hosted enablement sessions as the primary awareness and demand generation vehicle for the EMEA ecosystem. Build hands-on demonstration environments and interactive experiences that partners can use independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intervene directly on the highest-value partner-attached deals across EMEA: co-sell calls, technical discovery, PoV scoping, architecture review, and technical win support. Own the engagement until the partner’s team can carry it independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transform bespoke partner enablement sessions into structured LMS modules and certification tiers that scale across the EMEA partner base without requiring live PDE support for each new partner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce “better together” reference architectures for strategic partner combinations across cloud providers and AI platforms. Include deployment diagrams, network topology, IAM patterns, and operational runbooks that partner SAs can hand directly to customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Codify each successful partner engagement into a repeatable GTM play: trigger conditions, discovery questions, positioning framework, demo script, PoV scope template, and expected outcomes. Build a playbook library that a new PDE or partner seller can pick up and run.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI-powered self-service tools that automate high-volume PDE activities: Opportunity Brief Generator, PR/FAQ Generator, Workshop-in-a-Box deployment, and demo site builder.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce a monthly partner intelligence digest from EMEA engagements: what customers are asking for, how competitors are positioning, where integrations are missing, which vertical use cases are emerging. Distribute to Product, Engineering, and GTM leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the EMEA-relevant portions of the joint technical integration roadmap with strategic partners. Define priorities cross-functionally with Product and Engineering based on field signals from the EMEA market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and publish Partner Relations content, the ecosystem equivalent of Developer Relations: technical blog posts, cookbooks, partner ecosystem conference talks, enablement videos, and workshop recaps. Build Coder’s technical brand within the EMEA partner community.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to cloud marketplace product listing stewardship, competency maintenance documentation, and CSP co-build technical requirements as they apply to EMEA-specific partner and compliance contexts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in a combination of Forward Deployed Engineering, Solutions Architecture, Field CTO, Technical Consulting, or Developer Relations roles at an infrastructure, developer tools, or AI company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience helping partners or customers understand and adopt products in emerging or undefined categories, not just executing playbooks for established ones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven hands-on experience designing and deploying cloud infrastructure on at least one major cloud provider (AWS, Google Cloud, or Microsoft Azure), with production-level Kubernetes and Terraform depth. You have done the work and can speak to it with specificity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years deploying or operating AI coding agents in a production or near-production environment: you understand how agent loops execute, where credentials live, and what governance and audit requirements look like in a European enterprise context</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to articulate the architectural difference between workspace-local agent tooling and a centralized agentic harness, and to explain why that distinction matters to a security, compliance, or data sovereignty stakeholder</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with channel or technology partners in a co-sell model: hyperscaler partner programs, GSI/RSI partnerships, or VAR/distributor ecosystems in EMEA markets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building repeatable technical GTM assets that scaled beyond your personal delivery: sales plays, enablement curricula, reference architectures, or technical content programs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive communication and Field CTO credibility: you can hold a technical vision conversation with a partner CTO and a deal-level architecture review with an SE in the same day, in English and ideally at least one additional European language</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong written communication: you can produce a Working Backwards PR/FAQ, a technical architecture document, and a blog post without those being separate skills requiring separate people</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-directed, analytically minded, and comfortable operating with full autonomy. You will define processes that don’t exist, build tools that haven’t been scoped, and create a function from first principles in a new region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus Points</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>(Bonus tacos? That’s how we say thanks at Coder. Ask us about it.)</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior Forward Deployed Engineer experience at a platform company (Palantir, Scale AI, frontier AI lab, or equivalent embedded deployment model)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of public technical advocacy: blog posts, conference talks, open-source contributions, or developer/partner community engagement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with hyperscaler partner programs (e.g., ISV Accelerate, strategic collaboration agreements, co-sell programs) at an operational level</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with European regulatory environments: GDPR, DORA, NIS2, AI Act compliance requirements, and data sovereignty patterns for cloud-native deployments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with air-gapped or network-isolated deployments common in European financial services, government, or defense contexts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in AI governance frameworks, session audit requirements, or SIEM integration for AI workloads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with LLM gateway or proxy infrastructure (LiteLLM, OpenRouter, or equivalent) in a multi-team or enterprise context</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing human-in-the-loop breakpoints or escalation patterns for autonomous agent workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kubernetes certification (CKA, CKAD, or CKS)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Tailscale or similar overlay networking tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open-source contributions, particularly in CNCF, MCP, or AI agent ecosystems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Existing relationships with hyperscaler EMEA solutions architecture teams, European GSI technical practices, or AI infrastructure partner ecosystems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in German, French, or a Nordic language in addition to English</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have done the hard technical work before: deploying cloud-native infrastructure, navigating Kubernetes in production, building with Terraform, and operating in the complexity of large European enterprise environments. You bring that credibility into every partner conversation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You ca