ent fine-tuning of large-scale models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Algorithm Optimization:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optimize model inference for real-time robotic applications without compromising reasoning capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Publication &amp; Visibility:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the global research community by publishing high-impact papers at top-tier conferences (NeurIPS, CVPR, ICRA, CoRL, etc.).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the Core Robotics and Hardware teams to integrate AI models into our physical platforms.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Academic Excellence:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PhD or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Robotics, or a related field, with a focus on Deep Learning and Computer Vision.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven Research Track Record:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant publications and citations at major conferences such as NeurIPS, CVPR, ICCV, ICRA, IROS, or CoRL.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional Background:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in leading AI research environments</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Mastery:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in PyTorch or JAX, experience with Transformers, Diffusion Models, and Large Language Models (LLMs).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Domain Knowledge:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of Vision-Language models and their application to Action/Control loops in robotics.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Location:</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zurich Area, Switzerland: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our Zurich office, offering a vibrant ecosystem for robotics and AI.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free meals at the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours and the option to work from home when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct collaboration with founders and world-leading AI experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to large-scale compute clusters and proprietary robotic datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A key role in shaping the future of embodied AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation and a relocation package for the Zurich area</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/sereact-gmbh/member-of-technical-staff-zurich-24981","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792885215},{"slug":"research-engineer-zurich-318019","company_name":"Sereact GmbH","title":"Research Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<h1>Research Engineer, Manipulation Data &amp; Teleoperation — Zurich</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role owns the data generation layer of Sereact's VLA stack: teleoperation systems and data collection infrastructure that feed Cortex, built from our Zurich research hub.</p><h2>About Sereact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sereact is a Series B embodied-AI company. Cortex, our VLA model, is deployed in live warehouse robotic cells across the EU and US. Zurich 