bot learning (UMI or a comparable system), not just operating one someone else built</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of retargeting algorithms for mapping human input onto robot hands or end-effectors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1 to 2 years of combined research, internship, or industry experience in robotics, mechatronics, or a related engineering discipline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software and systems engineering skills strong enough to build and maintain infrastructure other engineers rely on, not only research-grade prototypes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working as an individual contributor in a small, still-forming team</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A conference submission on manipulation, teleoperation, or retargeting where the candidate is an author (an MSc thesis submitted to a venue like CoRL counts; supervising a student team whose own work was later published does not)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teaching or TA experience in a robotics course</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some exposure to large-model training, even without an independent training record</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A concrete example of building something outside the formal role brief because the team needed it</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zurich Area, Switzerland: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our Zurich office, offering a vibrant ecosystem for robotics and AI.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free meals at the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours and the option to work from home when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct collaboration with founders and world-lead