 with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Overview:</strong><br />We're scaling fast across research, engineering, and deployment as Cortex, our vision-language-action model, moves into more live robotic cells across the EU and US. We're looking for a Senior Recruiter to own full-cycle recruiting for a portfolio of roles, working closely with hiring managers to build pipelines, run a rigorous process, and close strong candidates in a market where the best people have options. You'll operate with real autonomy over your reqs and be expected to build process, not just execute one handed to you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Responsibilities:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full-Cycle Recruiting &amp; Ownership</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own full-cycle recruiting for a portfolio of roles, from intake through offer, ensuring a consistent and high-quality candidate experience at every stage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage offer strategy and negotiation in partnership with hiring managers and leadership, keeping compensation and equity consistent with internal bands</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track time-in-stage across your pipelines and proactively unblock stalled candidates rather than waiting for a hiring manager to flag it</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring Manager Partnership &amp; Process Design</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner directly with hiring managers to define role requirements, calibrate the interview process, and align on what a strong hire actually looks like for each position</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and refine scorecards, structured interview kits, and screening criteria specific to each function you own</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach and calibrate interviewers on assessment standards, turning subjective impressions into structured, defensible hiring decisions</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pipeline &amp; Sourcing</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and manage a healthy, prioritized pipeline across inbound and outbound channels, balancing sourcing effort against proven high-yield channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run proactive outbound sourcing for specialist or hard-to-fill roles instead of relying on inbound alone</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage relationships with external agencies and vendors where used, including scoping engagements and monitoring fee exposure</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data &amp; Process</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate, up-to-date candidate and requisition data in Ashby, supporting reliable reporting on pipeline health, conversion rates, and time-to-hire</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flag process gaps or bottlenecks early, and contribute directly to the tools and playbooks the Talent function is still building out</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Education and Experience</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, ideally spanning both technical and non-technical hiring</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience recruiting in a startup or fast-growth environment, comfortable owning a high volume of live reqs with limited support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">No specific degree requirement; track record matters more than credentials</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skills</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong command of structured interviewing and competency-based assessment, not just informal impression-based screening</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to source and close passive candidates through outbound channels, not just manage what comes in</p></li><