&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/thgingenuity/managing-director-thg-studios-manchester-462957","tags":["Ingenuity Studios"],"job_types":[],"location":"Manchester","created_at":1792864522},{"slug":"senior-sales-executive-perform-by-marcus-evans-london-78800","company_name":"Marcus Evans","title":"Senior Sales Executive (Perform by Marcus Evans)","description":"<p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Marcus Evans</span></strong><span style="color:#242424"> is a global leader in business intelligence, helping our clients grow by making connections, sharing knowledge, inspiring people, building relationships and creating new opportunities. Since 1983, we have brought decision-makers together through high-level summits, conferences, online platforms and performance programmes, working across all sectors and regions.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">Our overriding approach is one of collaboration, and our belief that “We’ll be our most successful when we work together.” We recognise excellence and actively develop top performers into future leaders. Our culture promotes teamwork, continuous learning and global career growth.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">About Perform</span></strong></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">Perform by Marcus Evans is our performance-improvement consultancy. We don’t sell off-the-shelf training. We start with a diagnosis of what is actually holding a team or an organisation back, prescribe the programme that fixes it, deliver bespoke learning pathways facilitated by vetted trainers/coaches, and then assess what changed. Clients get a written view of the gaps, the fix and the result.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Job Summary</span></strong></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">We are hiring a Senior Sales Executives to sell Perform to senior leaders at large organisations: Heads of HR, L&amp;D, Talent and Transformation, and the business executives who sponsor their programmes. You will own the sale from first conversation to signed contract, working with our Programme Scientist, who builds the diagnosis and prescription behind every proposal. This is a consultative sale with long cycles, several stakeholders and meaningful deal values. We are looking for someone who has done it before and wants to build a book of business from the start.</span></p><p class="elementtoproof" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">This is an onsite role based in our </span><strong><span style="color:#242424">London </span></strong><span style="color:#242424">office.</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Key Responsibilities</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Generate and qualify your own pipeline through targeted outreach, networking, referrals and social selling to senior HR, L&amp;D and business leaders</p></li><li><p>Run structured discovery calls using our Initial Discovery Template, so the client’s real performance problem is clear before any proposal is written</p></li><li><p>Work with the Programme Scientist to turn discovery into a bespoke diagnosis, prescription and quote, and present it to the client sponsor</p></li><li><p>Position Perform as an expert advisor, qualify prospects rigorously, and manage intake so each quarter’s cohorts are full and the programme stays selective</p></li><li><p>Negotiate pricing and terms within our pricing framework, and take contracts through to signature</p></li><li><p>Keep every opportunity current in HubSpot CRM, from contact to lead to deal, so forecasting and reporting are accurate</p></li><li><p>Stay with the client after signature through delivery and assessment, and use the findings to open expansion and renewal conversations</p></li><li><p>Share what you learn from the market (objections, competitors, pricing pressure) with the leadership team so the offer keeps improving</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Qualifications</span></strong></p><p class="elementtoproof"><em><span style="color:#242424">Required:</span></em></p><ul><li><p>Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in Behavioural Science or related fields.</p></li><li><p>At least five years of B2B sales experience, including closing complex, high-value deals with multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p>Proven experience selling leadership development, learning and development, coaching, talent, HR consulting or other professional services to senior buyers</p></li><li><p>A record of meeting or exceeding targets, with examples you can discuss</p></li><li><p>Excellent written and spoken English, and the credibility to hold a conversation with a C-suite executive</p></li><li><p>Comfort with discovery-led, consultative selling rather than product pitching</p></li><li><p>Right to work in the UK</p></li></ul><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><em><span style="color:#242424">Preferred:</span></em></p><ul><li><p>Experience selling to financial services, banking, technology or other regulated, multinational clients</p></li><li><p>An existing network among HR and L&amp;D decision-makers</p></li><li><p>Experience working alongside subject-matter experts or consultants to build proposals</p></li><li><p>HubSpot, LinkedIn Sales Navigator or comparable CRM and prospecting tools</p></li><li><p>Additional languages</p></li></ul><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><em><span style="color:#242424">Marcus Evans</span></em></strong><em><span style="color:#242424"> is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity, and all employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit and business need.</span></em></p><p>#LI-Onsite</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/marcus-evans/senior-sales-executive-perform-by-marcus-evans-london-78800","tags":[],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, Greater London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792864305},{"slug":"product-management-director-soft-fm-estates-uk-312871","company_name":"Singu","title":"Product Management Director – Soft FM & Estates (UK)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About SINGU</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <strong>SINGU</strong>, we’re redefining how the world’s most ambitious real estate companies run their operations. Our mission is to become <strong>Europe’s leading platform </strong>for managing warehouse, logistics, retail, and multi-site commercial real estate portfolios — empowering our Clients to protect revenue, boost efficiency, and unlock new value across every aspect of their business.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our unified CAFM platform</strong> already powers the daily operations of <strong>over 250 million m² of real estate worldwide</strong>, supporting more than <strong>500,000 professionals.</strong> Following our union with the UK’s <strong>Micad</strong> and Germany’s <strong>net-haus,</strong> we now help manage <strong>100,000+ buildings</strong> across <strong>35+ countries</strong> — and we’re just getting started.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a leading growth equity investor, we’re scaling rapidly and partnering with global leaders such as<strong> Prologis, ECE, CTP, Hillwood,</strong> <strong>Logicor, GLP, and Unibail-Rodamco-Westfield.</strong> As we continue to grow through strategic acquisitions and bold innovation, we stay true to our core values: <strong>adaptability, collaboration, and client focus.</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re ready to help build Europe’s leading platform for property operations — and make a tangible impact on how the real estate industry works —<strong> join SINGU and be part of this transformation.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own a significant slice of the SINGU product suite: <strong>space management and Soft FM services</strong> – cleaning standards, portering, and catering – used every day primarily across the <strong>UK healthcare market</strong>. Product-market fit is established and thousands of users depend on these products daily. What the portfolio needs now is strategic direction and taking them to their next level of growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll do that through a <strong>team of four Product Managers</strong> who are domain experts in the products they run. This is a <strong>hands-on leadership role</strong>. You'll stay close to customer problems yourself, you'll raise the bar on how the team discovers and validates work, and you'll have real autonomy to decide what's worth building – and to prove it works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">SINGU group grows both organically and through acquisition, and several of these products arrived with the companies that built them. You'll shape the strategy for bringing them into <strong>one coherent ecosystem</strong> and lead your team through that change. If you enjoy taking a set of good but separate products and making them add up to something bigger, that is the interesting part of this job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll partner closely with Sales, Engineering, and Product colleagues across the SINGU Group so your portfolio drives revenue and solves real problems across the European FM market. <strong>AI is a must-have lever</strong> in our industry rather than a talking point: you'll be applying it where it measurably improves how our customers run their estates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>remote position</strong> <strong>with periodic travel to London and Kraków</strong> – roughly every two to four weeks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Role Scope</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>People Leadership &amp; Team Development:</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage and develop the Product Managers</strong> within the product team.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full management lifecycle: <strong>hiring, onboarding, mentorship, feedback, coaching, performance evaluations, promotions, and exits</strong>.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster a <strong>high-performing product culture</strong> based on customer empathy, data-driven decision-making, and outcome orientation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage staffing and focus areas across the suite, reallocating product resources where needed to balance discovery workload and meet strategic priorities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead the team through change</strong> – new ways of working, a shifting portfolio, and product consolidation – bringing people with you rather than around them.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Product Discovery &amp; Strategy:</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define and maintain product roadmaps</strong> aligned with business objectives, customer needs, and market trends.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide <strong>where to invest and where to hold</strong>: set a clear, defensible position on which initiatives scale and communicate it across the business.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong <strong>alignment with the Sales team</strong> to ensure product discovery and roadmap priorities actively unblock deals and support revenue growth.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and resolve ambiguities, dependencies, and competing priorities that impact discovery quality and speed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Product Management Best Practices &amp; Standards:</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Promote modern product practices, including <strong>continuous discovery, outcome-based roadmapping, and hypothesis-driven development</strong>.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure product teams consistently validate assumptions through <strong>user research, experimentation, and data analysis</strong>.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive improvements in requirements quality, stakeholder communication, prioritization frameworks, and release planning.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cooperate with the Chief Architect and Engineering Managers to ensure product decisions account for technical feasibility and platform constraints.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the adoption of <strong>AI-powered tools and analytics</strong> to improve product insights, customer understanding, and decision-making quality.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Collaboration &amp; Cross-Company Coordination:</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with commercial and customer-facing teams to align product strategy with <strong>go-to-market plans and revenue goals</strong> for the portfolio.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the company at <strong>external events, conferences, and industry forums</strong> to share product insights, build the Group's profile, and stay connected to market trends.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain alignment, knowledge sharing, and team cohesion with colleagues across the Group.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Experience &amp; Requirements</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must have's:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5+ years in product management</strong>, ideally with at least three of them in <strong>B2B SaaS</strong>. Strong B2C experience in FM, healthcare, or an adjacent domain is also worth a conversation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At least two years leading a team as a people manager</strong> – product managers ideally, but we are flexible on the setup; what matters is that you have owned a team, not that you are ready to start.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking a team or a product area through real change: new ways of working, a restructure, or <strong>post-acquisition integration</strong> – and bringing the sceptics with you.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrable experience <strong>applying AI within product development</strong>, using AI-powered tooling to accelerate discovery and delivery.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of <strong>leading product discovery</strong> across multiple methods and translating insights into validated roadmaps.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong commercial awareness</strong>: able to partner with Sales and align product decisions with revenue and retention goals.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data fluency</strong>: comfortable defining metrics, querying product analytics, and using quantitative evidence to drive decisions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellent stakeholder communication</strong>: able to frame trade-offs and build alignment across technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>English at C1 or above</strong>, written and spoken, with the confidence to represent the product externally.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have's:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in <strong>empowered product trios</strong> (or similar cross-functional squads) with engineering and design.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in <strong>healthcare (ideally the UK market, NHS)</strong>, public sector, or government-adjacent markets.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with <strong>platform or multi-product portfolio environments</strong>.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience <strong>integrating acquired products</strong> into a single coherent platform.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Polish or German alongside English</strong>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not sure you tick every box? If you are strong on product leadership and craft but light on one of the requirements, we would still like to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Here</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership:</strong> you own a portfolio and the team that runs it. Strategy, discovery, and outcomes are yours, not a backlog handed down to you.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Modern product culture:</strong> we work in trios, practice continuous discovery, and ship to learn.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI that makes sense:</strong> you'll apply AI to a platform customers already rely on, where it measurably improves how they run their estates – not bolted on for its own sake.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A stable base for ambitious work:</strong> SINGU is <strong>profitable and growing</strong>, with consistently stable results.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth:</strong> SINGU keeps growing through acquisition, so new areas to consolidate and lead keep appearing.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>International scope:</strong> <strong>five companies and around 250 people</strong> across Poland, the UK, and Germany, with a portfolio that spans markets rather than one office.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this role sounds like a good fit, we’d love to hear from you. Apply and help us build technology that supports critical operations every day.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/singu/product-management-director-soft-fm-estates-uk-312871","tags":["UK&I"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK","created_at":1792863613},{"slug":"security-engineer-london-326971","company_name":"Cuspai","title":"Security Engineer","description":"<h2>About CuspAI </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CuspAI is the frontier AI company on a mission to solve the breakthrough materials needed to power human progress. While nature took billions of years to perfect molecules, we are harnessing AI to unlock trillion-dollar materials breakthroughs in months, not millennia. Our founding team is the most cited in the world, comprised of world-class researchers in AI, chemistry and engineering.<br /><br />We are working on some of the hardest and most important challenges including energy, clean water, the future of compute, and carbon capture, and this is just the start of what our 'search engine' for next-generation materials will unlock.<br /><br />We invite you to be part of a diverse, innovative team at the intersection of AI and materials science, working to create impactful partnerships that drive innovation, scalability, and industry collaboration. This work matters. Your work matters.<br /><br /><strong>We’re on the cusp of the on-demand materials era. Join us.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Due to our rapid growth and the sensitivity of our proprietary materials discovery platform, we are seeking a Security Engineer to ensure our innovation happens at speed without compromising the safety of our IP or our users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your Impact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you will be building the automated security pipelines and AI-specific guardrails that protect our frontier models and research data, which is critical for maintaining the integrity of our materials discovery engine and the trust of our global partners.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an early security hire, you won't be a manual blocker; instead, you will architect a "shift-left" culture where security is a fundamental product feature. Your work ensures that as we scale our search for next-generation materials, our underlying infrastructure and world-class IP remain safely locked down.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-Specific Security &amp; IP Protection</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Secure the end-to-end ML lifecycle, implementing defenses against data poisoning and protecting our proprietary model weights from theft.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deploy prompt injection defenses and runtime firewalls to prevent unauthorized manipulation of our LLM interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement AI Security Posture Management (AI-SPM) to monitor and catalog self-hosted models, internal training datasets, and proprietary endpoints.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cloud Security, CI/CD &amp; Core DevSecOps</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Weave automated security “guardrails” directly into our CI/CD workflows, including secret scanning, API exposure checks, and software composition analysis (SCA).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Codify security policies using Infrastructure as Code (IaC), ensuring all cloud resources are automatically compliant with global standards (e.g. GDPR, SOC2).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage secrets and vulnerability patching for containerized environments (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes) to ensure our research environment is resilient.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design strict, least-privilege Identity and Access Management (IAM) controls to isolate sensitive training data and research workloads.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interdisciplinary Collaboration &amp; Security Culture</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead incident response efforts by monitoring production logs for anomalies and collaborating with AI Researchers to deploy rapid fixes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Empower the engineering team to own security by providing tools for local IDE security scanning and pre-commit hooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a security educator, cultivating a culture of shared responsibility across the AI, chemistry, and engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with researchers, chemists, and engineers to translate security requirements into practical workflows that support rather than slow down scientific work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Must Have Skills and Qualifications:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are motivated by the mission of using AI for planetary-scale impact and understand the high stakes of securing "deep tech" intellectual property.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience in a DevSecOps, Cloud Security, or Site Reliability Engineering role, preferably within a fast-paced startup or AI-centric company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building and securing CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or Jenkins).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong proficiency in Infrastructure as Code (e.g. Terraform, Pulumi) and securing cloud environments (AWS, GCP, or Azure).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of container security and orchestration (Docker, Kubernetes).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical knowledge of security frameworks and how to implement them without slowing down development cycles.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Bonus Points (But Not Critical):</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience with AI-specific security tools or defending against LLM-specific vulnerabilities (OWASP Top 10 for LLMs).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI Security Posture Management (AI-SPM) tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relevant certifications such as AWS Certified Security, CSEP, or OSCP.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A background or personal interest in materials science, chemistry, or the intersection of AI and physical sciences.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Additional Considerations</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role could be based in our <strong>Cambridge, London, Amsterdam</strong> or <strong>Berlin</strong> offices, with the expectation of being in the office three days per week. Additionally, there may be regular travel required to other locations for collaboration and project work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of your onboarding, you will be expected to spend at least a few weeks in our Cambridge/London office learning about our platform and getting to know us in person.<br /><br />Additionally, there may be regular travel required to Europe and other regional and global locations for collaboration and project work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A competitive salary:</strong> We value and reward impact and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity in CuspAI:</strong> You have a stake in the success of the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off to stay fresh:</strong> 28 days holiday (DE, NL, UK) or 21 days holiday (JP, SG, US), in addition to local public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>‘Gold Standard’ parental leave:</strong> 26 weeks (primary caregiver) and 12 weeks (secondary caregiver) at full pay - we look after you and your family while we work on the most important materials discovery problems together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional development budget:</strong> We invest in your career development so you can stay up to date with the latest industry knowledge or add to your skills to increase impact and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solve meaningful problems:</strong> See how your work has a direct impact on advancing materials science and solving sustainability and climate-related problems through the creation and application of bleeding-edge SOTA technology and revolutionary techniques</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True interdisciplinary teamwork:</strong> Be part of a deeply collaborative environment bridging AI research, computational chemistry, and experimental science - work with world-class researchers and engineers who enjoy sharing knowledge and supporting each other</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Join us in shaping the future of materials with AI. Together, we can create groundbreaking solutions for a more sustainable world.</strong><br /><br /><br /><strong>CuspAI is an equal opportunities employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace</strong>. We do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citizenship, marital, domestic or civil partnership status, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable law.<br /><br /><strong>We actively encourage applications from all backgrounds and value the unique perspectives and contributions that diversity brings to our team.</strong><br /><br /><strong>Please let us know if you require any specific adjustments during or after the interview process. We will do everything we can within reason to accommodate.</strong></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cuspai/security-engineer-london-326971","tags":["Platform & Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Cambridge, UK","created_at":1792863613},{"slug":"performance-engineer-london-237596","company_name":"Cuspai","title":"Performance Engineer","description":"<h2>About CuspAI </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CuspAI is the frontier AI company on a mission to solve the breakthrough materials needed to power human progress. While nature took billions of years to perfect molecules, we are harnessing AI to unlock trillion-dollar materials breakthroughs in months, not millennia. Our founding team is the most cited in the world, comprised of world-class researchers in AI, chemistry and engineering.<br /><br />We are working on some of the hardest and most important challenges including energy, clean water, the future of compute, and carbon capture, and this is just the start of what our 'search engine' for next-generation materials will unlock.<br /><br />We invite you to be part of a diverse, innovative team at the intersection of AI and materials science, working to create impactful partnerships that drive innovation, scalability, and industry collaboration. This work matters. Your work matters.<br /><br /><strong>We’re on the cusp of the on-demand materials era. Join us.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Due to the rapid scaling of our compute requirements, we are seeking a Performance Engineer to serve as the vital bridge between our frontier AI models and our high-performance computing infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your Impact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you will be building the optimization layers and profiling infrastructure that maximizes the efficiency of our large-scale training and inference workloads, which is critical for accelerating our materials discovery pipeline and ensuring our researchers can iterate at the speed of thought.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">At CuspAI, compute is our most precious resource. Your main focus initially will be profiling our current training runs to identify bottlenecks in Model FLOP Utilization (MFU). Over time you are likely to get involved in designing custom kernels and low-level optimizations that allow us to train larger, more complex models for chemistry and physics that were previously computationally prohibitive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training &amp; Inference Optimization</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze model architectures to optimize how mathematical operations map onto hardware, specifically focusing on NVIDIA GPU kernels and collective communication layers (NCCL).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement state-of-the-art efficiency techniques such as quantization, model pruning, and distillation to lower latency for our materials “search engine” APIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Streamline data pipelines to ensure high-performance accelerators are never “starved” for data during massive training runs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Profiling, Observability &amp; Cost Management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use advanced observability tools to trace end-to-end execution of training jobs, pinpointing exact locations of processing clogs or interconnect contention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain real-time dashboards tracking vital system metrics, including MFU, memory bandwidth utilization, and cluster uptime.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and justify the utilization of our AI accelerators (e.g. H100 clusters), preventing idle time and memory leaks to ensure every dollar of compute spend translates into scientific progress.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop scaling laws and internal tools to predict system behavior across compute, memory, and networking as our models grow in parameter count.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interdisciplinary Collaboration</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with AI Researchers to adapt model architectures for better hardware compatibility without sacrificing scientific accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Infrastructure team to influence the design of our future compute clusters based on performance data and profiling results.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Must Have Skills and Qualifications:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are someone who gets excited about the opportunity to enable scientists to work on world changing challenges in this domain, with a personal interest in the potential applications of the technology that Cusp is building.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 3+ years of experience in performance engineering, site reliability engineering, or low-level software development, specifically focused on high-performance computing (HPC) or AI workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert-level knowledge of GPU architecture and experience optimizing CUDA kernels or using libraries like Triton.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of distributed training frameworks (e.g. PyTorch Distributed, DeepSpeed, or Megatron-LM) and networking protocols.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in profiling tools such as Nsight Systems, Nsight Compute, or Weights &amp; Biases for performance tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A "builder" mindset with the ability to work autonomously in an early-stage, fast-paced startup environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Bonus Points (But Not Critical):</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with specialized AI hardware such as TPUs or alternative accelerators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An academic background or personal interest in Materials Science, Chemistry, or Physics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of MLOps practices, specifically regarding the deployment of models at scale in cloud environments (AWS/GCP/Azure).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributions to open-source performance optimization or machine learning libraries.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Additional Considerations</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role could be based in our <strong>Cambridge, London, Amsterdam</strong> or <strong>Berlin</strong> offices, with the expectation of being in the office three days per week. Additionally, there may be regular travel required to other locations for collaboration and project work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of your onboarding, you will be expected to spend at least a few weeks in our Cambridge/London office learning about our platform and getting to know us in person.<br /><br />Additionally, there may be regular travel required to Europe and other regional and global locations for collaboration and project work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A competitive salary:</strong> We value and reward impact and growth</p>