800M+ in ARR.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 1000+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>⭐️ Why we are hiring ⭐️ </strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re opening an <strong>Enterprise</strong> <strong>Sales Team Lead</strong> role in France to <strong>lead a growing team of 4 Senior Account Executives,</strong> who are in charge of acquiring customers <strong>with more than 3,000 employees, including all CAC40 companies.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will <strong>own acquisition on the Enterprise segment in France</strong> and <strong>run the business end‑to‑end</strong>: you will be <strong>hands-on on the field</strong> while <strong>coaching and scaling</strong> a team of Account Executives to win this market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This position sits at the heart of our growth ambition: We have just passed the one million member milestone – and this is only the beginning! We’re accelerating acquisition in France and doubling down on our portfolio — and the <strong>Enterprise segment is one of the core pillars of that plan</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Enterprise segment</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perimeter:</strong> companies of 3000+ employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Verticals:</strong> all Verticals (Tech, Retail, Industrial Companies etc)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Total Addressable Market:</strong> ~<strong>7M members</strong> in France</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Enterprise Sales is exciting at Alan</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diverse workforce</strong>: Mix of 60% cadres / 40% non-cadres, often with subsidiaries or multi-site operations, ranging from highly tech-savvy employees to those requiring digital adoption support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Critical challenges</strong>: <strong>Multi-stakeholder decision processes</strong> involving HRD, CFO, CEO, Payroll, CSE, Legal, Purchasing, Comp &amp; Ben, Accounting, Brokers, Unions, <strong>long sales cycles</strong> (multi-year conversations), RFP processes requiring deep audits and product customization, and strong influence from unions/CSE who can co-manage health insurance topics;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Company profiles</strong>: Flagship companies (widely known brands), groups with standalone entities or subsidiaries, often with focus on employee wellbeing (QVT programs, Great Place to Work), modern company culture, and strategic communication about digitization or employer brand attractiveness;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR priorities</strong>: Increasing productivity, obtaining fair and competitive pricing, contributing to employee well-being through customized health plans, simplifying HR processes with digital platforms, and managing change management concerns when implementing new health insurance (biggest fear for large companies)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Critical business characteristics</strong>: This segment requires <strong>breadth &amp; depth of expertise</strong> to navigate complex organizations, <strong>account-based strategies</strong> with Key Account Management approach, early engagement in company roadmaps, face-to-face meetings, co-creation of insurance and digital products (tailored offers considering past results, specific regimes, demographics, payroll system integration), and ability to work through RFPs and with brokers. Sales cycles are <strong>volatile</strong> with high stakes: 1 deal = 50% of annual target for Enterprise Account Executives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our approach for Enterprise companies positions Alan as a <strong>strategic partner in health</strong> rather than just an insurance provider, emphasizing our digital platform for fluid UX, customized health plans at fair pricing, and health/well-being services. Success requires leveraging high-level connections, building professional materials, and potentially creating exclusive "Health Clubs" or labels for early adopters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>⭐ What you will do ⭐</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the <strong>Sales leader</strong> of the Enterprise Sales team in France, responsible for both <strong>hitting the numbers</strong> and <strong>scaling the machine</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">More precisely, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the Enterprise acquisition plan in France.</strong> Design and execute the go‑to‑market strategy for 3000 employee customers, from targeting to closing, to <strong>reach ambitious acquisition targets and scale the segment</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead &amp; coach a team of 4 Account Executives</strong> (and likely more to come)</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive <strong>hiring, onboarding, and career development</strong> as we scale the crew and the segment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help each team member reach their targets with <strong>clear expectations</strong>, <strong>rigorous follow‑up</strong>, and <strong>ongoing coaching</strong> on methodology, deal execution, and pipeline management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be <strong>on the field with the team</strong>: prospecting, joining key meetings, supporting tough negotiations, and owning <strong>strategic opportunities</strong> to maximize win rates.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Empower every member of the team:</strong> Create the conditions for everyone to <strong>reach and exceed their goals</strong>: strong feedback culture, coaching, clear ownership, and autonomy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ensure market fit and remove blockers:</strong> Surface customer expectations, patterns, and blockers, and ensure they’re addressed through the right <strong>strategic and execution plans</strong> (product, pricing, ops, marketing, etc.).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">For this opportunity, we are aiming to hire within the F-G<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity"> <u>level range</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>⭐ Is it what you are looking for? ⭐</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You may be a great fit at Alan if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>at least 10 years experience in B2B sales</strong>, with a <strong>proven track record of hitting and exceeding targets</strong> as an Account Executive and Sales Leader</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have <strong>experience leading and coaching sales teams</strong>, with the ability to set a <strong>high bar</strong>, give <strong>clear direction</strong>, and <strong>help people grow</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have full working proficiency<strong> in French</strong>, and advanced level in <strong>English</strong> for internal communication</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a very <strong>hands‑on mentality</strong>: you love being on the field with your team, joining customer meetings, helping on tough negotiations, and sharing what works</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experience <strong>selling to Enterprise level companies (3000+ employees and above)</strong> in <strong>multi‑stakeholder deals</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable operating in <strong>fast‑paced, ambiguous environments</strong>, and