ions; promptly notifying the Production Manager and Technical Support (Olivier); assisting with the initial diagnosis of straightforward technical issues.</p><p>- On-Site Presence & Operational Continuity: Ensuring production continuity at the assigned site and participating in shift handovers between teams, as well as during Technical Support interventions.</p><h2>What we are looking for</h2><p>We are looking for someone ready to take on the operation of our specialized laser ablation equipment within our agile team. </p><ul><li><p>Open to working 4 nights/week</p></li><li><p>German and English speaker</p></li><li><p>Willing to travel in Germany and within Switzerland ( at our cost)</p></li></ul><h2>Your first months at nu glass</h2><p>You will quickly get hands-on with state-of-the-art laser technology, integrating into our daily operations and contributing to projects that enhance connectivity and sustainability. If you match most of our requirements, we encourage you to apply.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>Flexible working hours</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p>CHF 60,000–64,800 per year</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/nu-glass/robot-pilot-spiez-149435","tags":["Automation Engineering"],"job_types":["Fixed-term contract (befristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Spiez","created_at":1792647035},{"slug":"remote-seo-digital-marketing-specialist-switzerland-427846","company_name":"Pavago","title":"SEO & Digital Marketing Specialist","description":"<h2><strong>SEO &amp; Digital Marketing Specialist – Technical SEO, Google Ads &amp; Lead Generation | Remote</strong></h2><p><strong>Position Type:</strong> Full-Time, Remote<br> <strong>Working Hours:</strong> U.S. Business Hours<br> <strong>Experience Level:</strong> Mid-Level to Senior<br> <strong>Department:</strong> Digital Marketing / Growth Marketing</p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p>At Pavago, one of our clients is hiring an experienced <strong>SEO &amp; Digital Marketing Specialist</strong> to develop, execute, and optimize digital marketing strategies that increase organic traffic, improve search rankings, generate qualified leads, and drive measurable business growth.</p><p>The ideal candidate has strong expertise in <strong>technical SEO, Google Ads, paid social advertising, content optimization, marketing analytics, and automation</strong>. This is a hands-on role requiring someone who can independently manage campaigns, identify growth opportunities, and turn marketing data into actionable strategies.</p><p>You’ll take ownership of organic search performance, paid advertising, website optimization, and lead generation while exploring emerging opportunities in <strong>AI-powered search optimization (AEO/GEO)</strong>.</p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><strong>SEO Strategy &amp; Optimization</strong></h3><ul><li>Develop and execute SEO strategies to improve organic visibility, keyword rankings, and website traffic.</li><li>Conduct keyword research, competitor analysis, and search intent analysis.</li><li>Perform technical SEO audits, addressing indexing, crawling, site architecture, page speed, and mobile performance.</li><li>Optimize meta titles, descriptions, headings, internal linking, URLs, and structured data.</li><li>Execute ethical link-building strategies and monitor search algorithm updates.</li><li>Optimize content for traditional search engines and AI-powered search experiences (AEO/GEO).</li></ul><h3><strong>Paid Advertising &amp; Lead Generation</strong></h3><ul><li>Plan, launch, and optimize campaigns across <strong>Google Ads, Meta Ads, and LinkedIn Ads</strong>.</li><li>Manage advertising budgets to improve lead quality, Cost per Lead (CPL), and Return on Ad Spend (ROAS).</li><li>Develop and optimize landing pages, lead capture forms, and conversion funnels.</li><li>Implement retargeting and remarketing campaigns.</li><li>Collaborate with sales teams to align marketing initiatives with revenue goals.</li></ul><h3><strong>Content Marketing &amp; Website Management</strong></h3><ul><li>Develop SEO-driven content strategies aligned with business objectives.</li><li>Create and optimize website copy, blog articles, and landing pages.</li><li>Manage website updates through <strong>WordPress, Webflow, or similar CMS platforms</strong>.</li><li>Collaborate with designers, developers, and content creators to improve website performance and user experience.</li></ul><h3><strong>Analytics, Reporting &amp; Optimization</strong></h3><ul><li>Monitor traffic, keyword rankings, conversions, and campaign performance using <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4), Google Search Console, and Google Tag Manager</strong>.</li><li>Build performance dashboards and provide actionable marketing reports.</li><li>Conduct A/B testing across landing pages, advertisements, and campaigns.</li><li>Analyze user behavior and identify opportunities to improve conversion rates.</li></ul><h3><strong>Marketing Automation &amp; CRM</strong></h3><ul><li>Manage email marketing campaigns, lead nurturing sequences, and automated workflows.</li><li>Work with platforms such as <strong>HubSpot, GoHighLevel, Salesforce, or ActiveCampaign</strong>.</li><li>Improve lead tracking, marketing attribution, and sales handoffs.</li><li>Maintain accurate campaign data and performance reporting.</li></ul><h2><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></h2><ul><li><strong>3+ years of professional experience</strong> in SEO, digital marketing, or performance marketing.</li><li>Proven success improving organic rankings, website traffic, and qualified lead generation.</li><li>Strong knowledge of <strong>technical SEO, on-page SEO, off-page SEO, and content optimization</strong>.</li><li>Hands-on experience with <strong>GA4, Google Search Console, Google Tag Manager, SEMrush, Ahrefs, or similar tools</strong>.</li><li>Experience managing <strong>Google Ads and paid social media campaigns</strong>.</li><li>Familiarity with WordPress, Webflow, or other CMS platforms.</li><li>Understanding of conversion rate optimization (CRO), landing pages, and lead generation funnels.</li><li>Experience with CRM and marketing automation platforms.</li><li>Strong analytical skills and ability to translate data into actionable improvements.</li><li>Excellent written and verbal English communication skills.</li><li>Ability to independently manage multiple campaigns and meet deadlines.</li><li>Availability during <strong>U.S. Business Hours</strong>.</li></ul><h2><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h2><ul><li>Experience with <strong>Answer Engine Optimization (AEO)</strong> and <strong>Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)</strong>.</li><li>Knowledge of local SEO and Google Business Profile optimization.</li><li>Familiarity with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and technical website improvements.</li><li>Experience in B2B marketing, SaaS, professional services, or lead-generation businesses.</li><li>Experience with Looker Studio and advanced marketing reporting.</li><li>Certifications in Google Ads, Google Analytics, HubSpot, or SEO.</li></ul><h2><strong>What Makes You a Strong Fit</strong></h2><ul><li>You take ownership of marketing performance and focus on measurable results.</li><li>You understand how SEO, paid advertising, content, and conversion optimization work together.</li><li>You can independently develop strategies, execute campaigns, and analyze performance.</li><li>You’re proactive about identifying growth opportunities and testing improvements.</li><li>You stay informed about search engine updates and emerging AI-powered marketing trends.</li><li>You communicate clearly and collaborate effectively with remote teams.</li></ul><h2><strong>What a Typical Day Looks Like</strong></h2><p>Your day may begin by reviewing <strong>GA4, Goo