ic materials requirements and material inventory across our products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate chemical stability, ageing and environmental sensitivity to define safe-for-use, storage and operational requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and oversee material qualification in line with NATO standards, internally and with external partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run hands-on material characterization and build the laboratory capability, in-house or through partners, to support it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess supplier specifications, process capability and quality requirements to ensure repeatability and traceability, and manage inspections and non-conformances.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support warhead and fuze engineers in sourcing and preparing materials for prototype testing, and report results to systems engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build qualification frameworks and guidance for the wider team, and contribute to growing an internal materials team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s degree or PhD in Chemistry, Materials Science, Chemical Engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of explosive materials, propellants and pyrotechnics, including explosive safety and hazardous materials handling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with analytical techniques such as DSC, TGA, FTIR and Raman spectroscopy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience characterizing and evaluating materials in accordance with NATO qualification standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running qualification programs for materials used in pyrotechnic or energetic systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understandin